# The OpenAlex snapshot partition (815 MB). Not committed: it is a public,
# immutable artefact addressable by release date, so committing it would bloat
# the repo without adding reproducibility. R/snapshot.R fetches it on demand and
# the release is pinned (SNAPSHOT_RELEASE), which is what actually makes the
# extraction reproducible.
data/snapshot/
*.parquet

# Rendered output. The .md source and the Makefile are the artefacts; the PDF is
# a build product and `make proposal` regenerates it (and fails on a third page).
proposal/*.pdf
proposal/*.aux
proposal/*.log

# Node
app/node_modules/
app/.next/
app/out/
.DS_Store

# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# Scratch
*.tmp

# Saved-webpage asset dumps (JS/CSS/images from the call-for-proposals and
# Scholar pages). The readable source is kept; the scraped chrome is not.
documentation/*_files/
documentation/*.html
documentation/*.htm
# The screening inputs and labels ARE the study. findings 09-13 all read
# canadian_sample.rds, so excluding it would mean a fresh clone cannot run
# `make pilot-offline` -- and the proposal's central reproducibility claim
# would be false. 3.1 MB is a fine price for that claim being true.
.gstack/

# Secrets. The repo is going public. `.env` carries the OpenAI/xAI/Anthropic keys
# and deploy/.dbpass the Postgres password; both showed as UNTRACKED-BUT-NOT-IGNORED
# in `git status`, which is one `git add -A` away from publishing them.
.env
.env.*
deploy/.dbpass
deploy/*.dbpass

# Build products.
build/
protocol/*.pdf
logs/

# The local DuckDB/Postgres materialisation of the frame. Rebuilt by R/, not a source.
data/db/

# Harvest bookkeeping: machine-written, regenerated by R/harvest_frame.R.
data/frame/partitions_done.txt
data/frame/s3_listing.txt

# The live site's dependencies and build output. `app/node_modules/` was ignored and
# `site/` was not, so 19,217 files of node_modules and a .next build were committed
# into a repo that is about to be public. Ignore the CONTENT, not the directory.
site/node_modules/
site/.next/
site/out/
site/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
